issues.suggestedFix:
Assign unconditionally so the flag is fully re-derived every render:

function resetSilentForRegion(
    el: Element,
    regionModel: RegionModel
): void {
    // @ts-ignore FIXME:TS fix the "compatible with each other"?
    el.silent = !!regionModel.get('silent');
}

Verified: this makes the stale-refresh and cross-instance probes pass and leaves all 27 existing geo/map/api unit tests green. (If you also want region-level `silent` to be strictly opt-in rather than inheriting `geo.silent`/`series.silent` through `parentModel`, use `regionModel.getShallow('silent', true)` instead — component/series-level `silent` is already applied separately by GeoView (`mapDraw.group.silent`) and echarts.ts (`chartView.group.silent`).)

Add test/ut/spec/component/geo/regionSilent.test.ts and test/ut/spec/chart/map/regionSilent.test.ts modelled on the existing geoJSONRegionStyle.test.ts helpers, asserting:
(1) geo GeoJSON: regions:[{name:'AAA', silent:true}] -> region group `.silent === true`, 'BBB' group `.silent === false`;
(2) series.map GeoJSON: data:[{name:'AAA', silent:true}] -> `data.getItemGraphicEl(idx).silent === true`, sibling false;
(3) update map data: setOption again with the same region but no `silent` -> el.silent === false (this is the case that currently fails for SVG);
(4) SVG-backed map (registerMap(name, {svg: '<svg><rect name="AAA"/><rect name="BBB"/></svg>'})): silent toggles true -> false across setOption, for both geo.regions and series.map data items.

Assign unconditionally so the flag is fully re-derived every render:

function resetSilentForRegion(
    el: Element,
    regionModel: RegionModel
): void {
    // @ts-ignore FIXME:TS fix the "compatible with each other"?
    el.silent = !!regionModel.get('silent');
}

Verified: this makes the stale-refresh and cross-instance probes pass and leaves all 27 existing geo/map/api unit tests green. (If you additionally want region-level `silent` to be strictly opt-in rather than inheriting `geo.silent`/`series.silent` through `parentModel`, use `regionModel.getShallow('silent', true)` — component/series-level `silent` is already applied separately by GeoView via `mapDraw.group.silent` and by echarts.ts via `chartView.group.silent`.)
